    {
      "id": "0f517d4b7ab8-q1",
      "number": 1,
      "question": "In &Delta;PQR, M, N, and S are the mid-points of sides PQ, PR, and QR, respectively. If the area of &Delta;PQR is 46 cm&sup2;, what is the area (in cm&sup2;) of the quadrilateral MNRQ?",
      "questionHtml": "In &Delta;PQR, M, N, and S are the mid-points of sides PQ, PR, and QR, respectively. If the area of &Delta;PQR is 46 cm&sup2;, what is the area (in cm&sup2;) of the quadrilateral MNRQ?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "39",
          "html": "39"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "27.6",
          "html": "27.6"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "23",
          "html": "23"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "34.5",
          "html": "34.5"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p>Area of ΔPQR = 46 cm<sup>2</sup></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-family: var(--bs-body-font-family); font-size: var(--bs-body-font-size); font-weight: var(--bs-body-font-weight); text-align: var(--bs-body-text-align);\">Area of each smaller triangle = 46 / 4 = 11.5 cm</span><sup style=\"font-family: var(--bs-body-font-family); font-weight: var(--bs-body-font-weight); text-align: var(--bs-body-text-align);\">2</sup></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-family: var(--bs-body-font-family); font-size: var(--bs-body-font-size); font-weight: var(--bs-body-font-weight); text-align: var(--bs-body-text-align);\">Area of quadrilateral MNRQ = 3 × 11.5 = 34.5 cm</span><sup style=\"font-family: var(--bs-body-font-family); font-weight: var(--bs-body-font-weight); text-align: var(--bs-body-text-align);\">2</sup></p>\n",
